iables are in scope for the entire block of logic by placing the let-binding outside the braces; unlike previous failed attempts, it changes the scoping structure rather than inlining or only moving let-bindings.\n\n[LESSON]:\nAlways ensure that let-bound variables in Alloy are introduced at the outermost block that needs to reference them, and that all relevant logic is syntactically inside their scope.",
