sue type: requirement ambiguity (now resolved)\n- Issue: Previous ambiguity in R2 regarding timing of transition to NormalMode after Emergency mode ended; specifically, whether restoration must be synchronous, permissive up to endedAt, or may be delayed. User has now selected the \"no later than endedAt\" option.\n- Rationale: Ambiguity led to repeated assertion failures and model repairs; explicit user selection resolves the requirement gap.\n- Action: Update the requirement and model to match clarified semantics; confirm that the assertion and model enforce \"restoration to NormalMode no later than endedAt\".\n\n=== ASSUMPTIONS REVIEW ===\n- Assumption: \"For every EmergencyTrigger, there exists a State at endedAt in the same session where the mode is NormalMode, and for all States at or after endedAt, mode is NormalMode.\"\n- Category: need confirmation (now clarified)\n- Rationale: User has confirmed permissive restoration—system may return to NormalMode before or at endedAt, but not after; update model and documentation accordingly.\n\n=== REQUIREMENT UPDATES ===\n- Affected Requirement/Assumption/Constraint: R2: Emergency Mode Duration (SYSTEM OVERVIEW, R2), and assertion assertR2_EventualReturnToNormal.\n- Issue Type: ambiguity (now resolved)\n- Evidence: Three consecutive failed model repair attempts; assertion failures; user-provided clarification.\n- Recommended Update: Replace R2 requirement text with:\n    \"For every EmergencyTrigger, the system MUST return to NormalMode no later than EmergencyTrigger.endedAt in the corresponding session, and remain in NormalMode for all subsequent times in that session.\"\n- Implication: System is now permitted to transition to NormalMode before or exactly at endedAt, but not after; assertion and model must match this behavior for correct verification.\n\n=== UPDATED USER QUESTIONS ===\nNone\n\n=== Q&A STATUS UPDATE ===\nNone - no status changes\n\n=== HANDOFF TO RE ===\nPriority 1 (Critical blockers): Update R2 requirement and assertion to enforce \"no later than endedAt\" restoration semantics; revise model and re-verify.\nPriority 2 (Important improvements): Confirm assertion passes with updated requirement; document requirement clarification in specification and model comments.\nPriority 3 (Optional enhancements): Review additional edge cases or negative scenarios (e.g., restoration just before endedAt) after successful re-verification.\n```",
