    "evaluator_feedback": "```\n=== NEXT ACTION DECISION ===\nDecision: refine/narrow fix\nRationale: User review clarified critical requirements (global Emergency mode, system-wide privilege, required delegations, and administrator clearance). The model and tests must be updated to reflect these clarifications for meaningful verification.\n\n=== VERIFICATION STATUS ===\n- Syntax: OK\n- Baseline: Satisfiable\n- Combined Model: Satisfiable\n- Assertions: Pass\n- Instances: Suspicious (lack of global Emergency mode and required delegations)\n- Vacuity: Possible (underconstrained scenarios and vacuous assertion passing)\n\n=== CONVERGENCE_RECOMMENDATION ===\nStatus: FALSE\nReasoning: User clarified global Emergency semantics and invariants, and requested additional delegation scenarios. Current model and tests do not yet enforce these; further targeted refinement and coverage are required.\n\n=== REPAIR INSTRUCTIONS ===\n1. Rework the model so that Emergency mode is a global/system-wide state, not per session. All active sessions must be in the same mode (either all in Emergency or all in Normal), and only one Emergency may be active at a time.\n   - Replace any session-local Emergency mode/state predicates/facts with a single global EmergencyMode indicator.\n   - Add a fact enforcing that all sessions share the same mode at any time.\n   Example:\n   ```\n   one sig SystemState {\n     mode: one Mode,\n     sessions: set Session,\n     ...\n   }\n   fact AllSessionsShareMode {\n     all s: Session | s.mode = SystemState.mode\n   }\n   ```\n2. Add a fact prohibiting more than one EmergencyTrigger (i.e., only one active Emergency at any time).\n   Example:\n   ```\n   fact SingleActiveEmergency {\n     lone et: EmergencyTrigger | et.active = True\n   }\n   ```\n3. Remove or adjust any logic allowing administrators to acquire Emergency privileges in multiple sessions or independently. Emergency privileges and policy relaxations must apply globally and be revoked globally.\n   - Remove per-session emergency privilege assignment.\n   - Add assertions/facts ensuring privilege assignment is system-wide.\n4. Add a positive test predicate and run to ensure at least one role delegation occurs during Emergency mode AND at least one in Normal mode.\n   Example:\n   ```\n   pred TestDelegationCoverage {\n     some s1: State | s1.mode = EmergencyMode and some d1: Delegation | d1 in s1.delegations\n     some s2: State | s2.mode = NormalMode and some d2: Delegation | d2 in s2.delegations\n   }\n   run TestDelegationCoverage for ...\n   ```\n5. Update revocation and restoration assertions to refer to the global Emergency state and system-wide privilege, not per-session.\n6. Update the model to make \"all administrators have high clearance\" a hard system invariant (fact), but allow for high-clearance users who are not administrators.\n   Example:\n   ```\n   fact AdminsHaveHighClearance {\n     all a: Administrator | a in HighClearanceUsers\n   }\n   ```\n7. Retest all Emergency mode triggers, privilege assignments, revocations, and role delegations under the new global mode model. Add positive runs for Emergency entry/exit, privilege transitions, and delegation/revocation edge cases.\n\n=== POTENTIAL REQUIREMENT ISSUES ===\n- Issue type: requirement gap\n- Issue: Previous requirements allowed for per-session Emergency state and privileges, but system behavior is now clarified as global. Requirements and model must be updated for this system-wide invariant.\n- Rationale: The previous ambiguity led to underconstrained, misaligned model behavior and verification.\n- Action: Update requirement language for Emergency mode, privilege assignment, and revocation to be global/system-wide, not per session.\n\n- Issue type: missing requirement\n- Issue: Requirement to guarantee that at least one role delegation occurs during both Emergency and Normal modes for verification completeness.\n- Rationale: Without this, revocation and delegation assertions/tests may pass vacuously.\n- Action: Specify in requirements and test cases that at least one delegation must occur in each mode for adequate verification.\n\n=== ASSUMPTIONS REVIEW ===\n- Assumption: Administrators always have high clearance, but not all high-clearance users are administrators.\n- Category: keep (confirmed as strict system invariant)\n- Rationale: User confirmed this as a hard invariant; model must enforce accordingly.\n\n=== REQUIREMENT UPDATES ===\n- Affected Requirement/Assumption/Constraint: Emergency mode/privilege assignment (R3.3 and related)\n- Issue Type: ambiguity / logical gap\n- Evidence: User clarification specifies Emergency mode is global, only one active Emergency at a time, and privileges are system-wide.\n- Recommended Update: Update all requirements and related constraints to state Emergency is a global/system-wide mode, with all sessions entering/exiting together, and privilege assignment/revocation is always global.\n- Implication: Model structure and test coverage must shift from per-session to system-wide logic; prevents vacuous or incorrect privilege scenarios.\n\n- Affected Requirement/Assumption/Constraint: Delegation during Emergency and Normal mode (R4.2 and related)\n- Issue Type: missing requirement\n- Evidence: User requires at least one delegation in both modes for meaningful verification of revocation logic.\n- Recommended Update: Add explicit requirement that at least one role delegation must occur during both Emergency and Normal modes (for verification).\n- Implication: Ensures model and tests cover delegation/revocation scenarios in all relevant system states.\n\n=== UPDATED USER QUESTIONS ===\nNone\n\n=== Q&A STATUS UPDATE ===\nNone - no status changes\n\n=== HANDOFF TO RE ===\nPriority 1 (Critical blockers): \n- Rework model and requirements to enforce global Emergency mode and privilege assignment/revocation (no per-session Emergency state).\n- Add positive test/run predicates to guarantee at least one delegation during both Emergency and Normal modes.\n- Update model to enforce \"all administrators have high clearance\" as a hard system invariant.\n\nPriority 2 (Important improvements): \n- Update revocation/restoration assertions and test scenarios to align with global Emergency semantics.\n- Add or update facts to prohibit more than one active Emergency at any time.\n- Add positive test scenarios for privilege transitions, delegation/revocation, and policy relaxation/restoration under global Emergency mode.\n\nPriority 3 (Optional enhancements): \n- Add edge-case test scenarios (e.g., early Emergency termination, delegation overlap).\n- Review assertion/test coverage for credential updates and privilege restoration order.\n```",
