y Normal mode state.\"\n     Implication: Makes explicit that Emergency-mode delegations may not persist into Normal mode, resolving the contradiction if R8.1 is made existential (see above).\n  \n  3. Affected Requirement/Assumption/Constraint: R3.3 (Emergency Privileges Assignment)\n     Issue Type: ambiguity\n     Evidence: Persistent counterexamples to the assertion that only triggering admins hold emergency privileges at all times during Emergency mode; requirement text does not specify if privilege handoff or transition overlap is permitted.\n     Recommended Update: R3.3 should state: \"Only the administrators who triggered Emergency mode may hold emergency privileges at any time during Emergency mode or in any Normal mode state; no other administrator may ever hold these privileges.\"\n     Implication: Clarifies privilege assignment boundaries and transition semantics, ensuring the assertion can be verified or the model adjusted accordingly."
