ction: Update the requirement to explicitly state that at least one delegation must be initiated and active during Emergency mode, and similarly for Normal mode, for verification purposes.\n\n- Issue type: requirement gap\n- Issue: Lack of requirement for recording revocation time and revoking admin for each delegation.\n- Rationale: User clarified that revocation must be auditable with these fields.\n- Action: Add requirement: \"The system must record the time and admin responsible for early revocation of any delegated role.\"\n\n=== ASSUMPTIONS REVIEW ===\n- Assumption: \"For verification purposes, at least one Emergency-mode delegation must occur during Emergency mode, and at least one Normal-mode delegation during Normal mode.\"\n- Category: keep\n- Rationale: User has explicitly confirmed this as the intended verification criterion.\n\n- Assumption: \"A delegation is active from delegation until its expiration or revocation by an admin; revocation time and admin are recorded.\"\n- Category: keep\n- Rationale: User confirmed and extended this operational definition.\n\n=== REQUIREMENT UPDATES ===\n- Affected Requirement/Assumption/Constraint: R8.1 (Delegation Coverage Verification)\n- Issue Type: ambiguity\n- Evidence: User explicitly clarified that at least one Emergency-mode delegation must occur during Emergency mode, and at least one Normal-mode delegation during Normal mode, for verification.\n- Recommended Update: \"For verification purposes, the model must ensure that at least one delegation is initiated and active during Emergency mode, and at least one delegation is initiated and active during Normal mode.\"\n- Implication: This removes the allowance for trivial (no delegation) executions during verification and aligns coverage predicates with explicit user intent.\n\n- Affected Requirement/Assumption/Constraint: Delegation revocation auditability\n- Issue Type: missing requirement\n- Evidence: User stated revocation time and admin must be recorded.\n- 