ow that all behaviors are possible, but not enforced in every trace.\n  \n  - Affected Requirement/Assumption/Constraint: Direct assignment and delegation preconditions (R5, baseline constraints)\n  - Issue Type: ambiguity/missing exception\n  - Evidence: Blocking instance generation when combined with mutex, clearance, and minimal user/role bounds.\n  - Recommended Update: \n    Add to the requirements:\n    \"For verification purposes, it is permissible for there to be executions in which not all users, roles, or administrators are assigned or able to delegate, provided that at least one scenario exists where the necessary assignments and delegations can occur to witness the required behaviors.\"\n  - Implication: This allows the model to admit executions where, due to assignment or global constraints, delegation is not possible, provided there is at least one witness execution for each desired behavior."
